<!--
  Brand mark: a shelf of books, and nothing else.

  **The shape.** Three upright books and one leaning, resting on a shelf plank. The three standing
  books share a baseline and near-aligned tops, and vary only in width and by a couple of units of
  height — a real row of books, not the deliberately staggered tops of a bar chart, which is what
  the first pass at this mark accidentally read as. The fourth book leans into the stack, resting
  its top against the third: that lean is the one gesture that says "books" rather than "bars",
  because nothing but a book stands at an angle on a shelf.

  The plank runs wider than the books on both sides, which is what turns a row of rectangles into
  "these books are *on a shelf*"; without the overhang the same shapes read as a fence.

  **Material 3 / adaptive-icon compliance.** The foreground and the monochrome layer are each a
  single 108dp vector, drawn straight into the full adaptive-icon canvas: no inset wrapper, no
  scaled-down "safe" sub-canvas, so every mask the system composes reads the mark at its intended
  size. Everything that carries the silhouette sits inside the 66dp safe-zone circle about the
  canvas centre: the extreme points are the plank's bottom corners (28,73) and (80,73) — radius
  √(26²+19²) ≈ 32.2 < 33 — so no launcher mask, however aggressive, cuts the shelf. There is no
  raster asset at any density; the same paths serve every tier.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- The books. Three spines standing on the plank's top edge at y=68, separated by a two-unit
         gap so the row never fuses into one block. Widths and heights differ just enough to read
         as separate volumes. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M33,42 L41,42 L41,68 L33,68 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M43,40 L50,40 L50,68 L43,68 Z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M52,43 L60,43 L60,68 L52,68 Z" />

    <!-- The leaning book: the same rectangle sheared four units off vertical, its top corner
         coming to rest against the right edge of the third book. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M64,68 L71,68 L67,41 L60,41 Z" />

    <!-- The shelf. A plain plank, overhanging the books by five units on each side. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M28,68 L80,68 L80,73 L28,73 Z" />
</vector>
